      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your MSA, you absolutely need a robust section on pricing, which should ideally include mechanisms for price adjustments, like a defined review period or a cap on increases. You must also nail down force majeure clauses to cover unexpected supply chain disruptions. Another crucial element is clear definitions of quality standards and inspection rights. Finally, ensure there are strong termination clauses that allow for exit if performance drops below agreed-upon levels.",
      "source": "target",
