      "content": "You're looking to guard against the *spirit* of the agreement, not just the letter, which is where things get thorny. You can address this by including broad \"cooperation\" or \"good faith performance\" covenants that require the supplier to act with integrity in all dealings. Furthermore, specify that any actions taken by the supplier, or their agents, that undermine the contract's intent—even if not explicitly prohibited—will constitute a material breach. This is your legal net to catch those slippery, underhanded tactics.",
